Metrics: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines metrics collection policy, standard metric categories,
  and project-specific metric selection rules.

Categories:
  RED (Service):
    - Rate: requests per second
    - Errors: error rate percentage
    - Duration: p50, p95, p99 latency

  USE (Infrastructure):
    - Utilization: CPU, memory, disk, network
    - Saturation: queue depth, connection pool
    - Errors: system error rate

  Business:
    - payment_attempts
    - payment_success
    - payment_failed
    - refund_attempts
    - refund_success
    - user_signups
    - active_sessions

  Security:
    - failed_login_attempts
    - rate_limit_hits
    - auth_failures
    - blocked_requests

CollectionRules:
  - Metrics MUST be collected for all production services
  - Business metrics MUST be defined per domain
  - Metric names MUST follow convention: <domain>_<action>_<status>
  - Tags/labels MUST include: service, environment, version, region

AlertIntegration:
  - Metrics feed into alerting engine
  - Thresholds defined in alerting.sdd
  - Business metric anomalies trigger incident review

State: +
  